  "id": "DrugBank_DB13931 - MONDO_5338",
  "verbalization": "Netarsudil is implicated in the pathogenesis of Open-angle Glaucoma through its association with Ocular Hypertension, a condition that is itself linked to multiple medications. The evidence suggests that Netarsudil may act as a mediator in the development of Open-angle Glaucoma by influencing Ocular Hypertension, which is a known risk factor for the condition. This connection is supported by the shared indication of Ocular Hypertension with both Befunolol and Dorzolamide, as well as with Latanoprostene Bunod, all of which are used in the treatment of glaucoma. The presence of these overlapping indications implies a potential mechanism by which Netarsudil could contribute to the development of Open-angle Glaucoma, possibly through its effects on intraocular pressure or other physiological processes. The consistent association across different pathways highlights the importance of Ocular Hypertension as a critical intermediate step in the relationship between Netarsudil and Open-angle Glaucoma.",
